# The Evidence Room — Project Rules

## Source of truth

1. Read `docs/MASTER_PLAN.md` before implementing any milestone work.
2. Read relevant supporting docs (`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`, `docs/CASE_001.md`, `docs/ROADMAP.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/TEST_PLAN.md`, `docs/PROGRESS.md`) before changing related systems.
3. Source-of-truth hierarchy: MASTER_PLAN → ARCHITECTURE → CASE_001 → DESIGN_SYSTEM → DECISIONS → existing code/tests → Cursor prompts.
4. Never silently change product requirements. If a prompt conflicts with the master plan, identify the conflict and stop for approval.

## Milestone discipline

5. Implement only the authorized milestone. Do not start the next milestone without explicit approval.
6. Stop at milestone boundaries and produce the milestone report format from `docs/MASTER_PLAN.md`.
7. Preserve the established architecture. Avoid unnecessary rewrites of working systems.
8. Do not expand scope without approval.

## Quality and honesty

9. Add tests for implemented behavior.
10. Run relevant verification for the milestone.
11. Never claim tests passed unless they were actually executed. Distinguish passed, failed, not executed, and blocked.
12. After each milestone, update `docs/PROGRESS.md` and record important decisions in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.

## Intellectual property and safety

13. Never use unauthorized RedHanded intellectual property (official logos, artwork, host likenesses, recordings, or copyrighted episode material).
14. Never commit or push without explicit authorization.
15. Do not delete unrelated files, reset Git history, force-push, or modify unrelated system configuration.
